"""loop-sdk — customer-side client for the Loop Source Bus.

Two layers:

* **High level (start here):** ``RobotStepSender`` — connect, send one
  named-reading dict per tick, disconnect. One class, three calls; the first
  send declares the channel layout, and ``declare`` is an optional fourth call
  for fixing it up front. It also handles robot config negotiation for you. Most
  control loops want only this.
* **Low level (shared core):** ``SourceProducer`` / ``SourceConsumer`` and the
  ``source.*`` domain types — the gRPC handshake, streaming, reconnection, and
  schema primitives the high-level sender is built on. Reach for these for a
  non-robot source kind or fuller control of the stream.
"""

